{"id": "319", "question": "How many wooden bars are on the front of the crib facing us?", "gt": "Nine; Nine bars; There are nine bars", "pred": "By examining the front of the crib facing the viewer, we can count the vertical wooden bars. Starting from the left and counting each bar, there are a total of 7 wooden bars visible on the front panel of the crib.", "group_key": "visual challenge", "sub_category": "visual challenge", "dataset": "haloquest", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "By examining the front of the crib facing the viewer, we can count the vertical wooden bars. Starting from the left and counting each bar, there are a total of 7 wooden bars visible on the front panel of the crib.", "cot": "[\"By examining the front of the crib facing the viewer, we can count the vertical wooden bars. Starting from the left and counting each bar, there are a total of 7 wooden bars visible on the front panel of the crib.\", \"Observing the front of the crib facing us, we can count the vertical wooden bars. Starting from the left and moving to the right, there are a total of 7 wooden bars forming the front guard of the crib.\\n\\nAnswer: 7\", \"Observing the front of the crib facing us, we can count the vertical wooden bars. There is one bar on the far left, followed by a gap, and then a series of five bars before the next gap. Continuing to the right of this gap, there are another five bars before the final bar on the far right. This gives a total of 1 + 5 + 5 + 1 = 12 bars.\\n\\nHowever, looking more closely at the image, the design appears to be symmetrical. There are two end posts on the far left and far right. Between these, there are two sets of vertical bars. If we count the bars between the left post and the right post, we can see there are 10 vertical bars in total (5 on the left side and 5 on the right side of the central space).\\n\\nTherefore, there are 10 wooden bars on the front of the crib facing us.\", \"Observing the crib from the front, we can count the vertical wooden bars. There is one bar on the far left, followed by a gap, then another bar, another gap, another bar, another gap, and finally a bar on the far right. Counting these bars from left to right, there are a total of 5 wooden bars on the front of the crib.\"]", "time_sec": 69.343, "generation_time_seconds": 69.1762, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0002, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 13.33, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
