{"id": "515", "question": "What do the English letters on the rock spell out?", "gt": "The letters on the rock are not in English.; The letters on the rock are in a different language.; They are not English.", "pred": "The English letters on the rock spell out \"Peace\".", "group_key": "false premises", "sub_category": "false premises", "dataset": "haloquest", "method": "base_sc", "raw_output": "The English letters on the rock spell out \"Peace\".", "cot": "[\"The English letters on the rock spell out \\\"Peace\\\".\", \"1. The image displays a large rock monument.\\n2. On the surface of this rock, there is a plaque with characters engraved on it.\\n3. The characters are not English letters; they are Japanese Kanji.\\n4. The characters are \\\"平和の丘\\\", which is read as \\\"Heiwa no Oka\\\".\\n5. \\\"Heiwa no Oka\\\" is the Japanese name for the site, which translates to \\\"Hiroshima Peace Memorial Park\\\" or \\\"Hiroshima Peace Mountain\\\".\\n6. Therefore, there are no English letters on the rock.\\n\\nThe answer is: There are no English letters on the rock.\", \"The image shows a large rock with the Japanese characters \\\"平和の丘\\\" inscribed on it. These characters are not English letters. Therefore, the question is based on a false premise; there are no English letters on the rock.\\n\\nNot present\", \"The image shows a large rock with Japanese characters carved into it. There are no English letters present on the rock.\"]", "time_sec": 45.797, "generation_time_seconds": 45.6484, "selection_time_seconds": 0.0001, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.29, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
